## Conclusion

Django is an opinionated framework that already implements several design patterns internally through its ORM, Middleware, and Signals system (Builder, Chain of Responsibility, Observer, and more). We should only manually add patterns that solve **business-specific logic** the framework has no opinion about (Strategy, State, Facade, Adapter, Command, Memento, Mediator, Prototype) — and avoid unnecessary abstraction layers (Abstract Factory, Flyweight, Visitor, Composite, Bridge) where the framework, or simpler code, already does the job.
